course: dictionary
lesson: 15210
title: Seniority: who is older, or has been longer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Seniority means being older or higher in rank than others. It can also mean how long someone has worked in a job. «In our school, Mrs Patel has the most seniority, because she has taught here for twenty years.» The words twenty years are the clue: she has been there longest, so she has the most seniority.
explain: Seniority often comes with rights. «In order of seniority, the oldest child chooses first.» Order and first are the clues. The oldest, or the person who has been in the job longest, goes ahead of the others.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «I'm the oldest, so I have seniority, so I go first.» That makes sense, so you have the right meaning. If the sentence stops making sense, try another meaning.
fact: Seniority means being older or higher in rank.
fact: Seniority can also mean how many years someone has worked in a job.
fact: Seniority can give a person more rights, such as choosing first.
fact: «Seniority» is a noun, and it is uncountable: you do not say «a seniority».
fact: A useful phrase is «in order of seniority», which means ranked from the oldest or longest-serving to the newest.
exercise: «In our school, Mrs Patel has the most seniority.» What does seniority mean here? | Being the youngest person in the room | *Having been there longest, or being highest in rank | Being the tallest | Having the least money in the school
exercise: «Children are chosen in order of seniority.» What does the phrase in order of seniority mean? | In alphabetical order by name | *From the oldest or longest-serving to the newest | From the shortest to the tallest | By picking names out of a hat
exercise: Which sentence uses seniority correctly? | I have seniority because I like pizza. | *The new teacher had less seniority than the head teacher. | The seniority was blue and very loud.
test: «Years of seniority» means the number of years someone has worked in a job. Which phrase is the best synonym for seniority in this sentence: «Her seniority meant she chose the room first»? | *Longer service and higher rank | A new pair of shoes | Being very small | Lots of shouting
test: Ben says, «I'm the oldest, so I have seniority, I go first.» What does Ben mean? | He has lost his seat and needs help. | He is the smallest in the class. | *He is older than the others, so he goes first. | He is the newest in the group, so he goes last.
exam: Which sentence shows seniority in the right way? | *After twenty years in the job, Mr Lee had the seniority to choose his own hours. | The seniority of the puppy made everyone laugh. | Seniority is the colour of the sky on a sunny day. | Seniority means running very fast in the park.
